				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				30
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add PostHog build telemetry and complete polyfill layer\n\nAdd a fire-and-forget PostHog build telemetry plugin to ESBuild configuration that captures:\n- Build duration, errors, and warnings\n- Compiler type (esbuild vs Rest)\n- Development vs production mode\n- User identifier for developer analytics\n\nAlso complete the Electron-to-Tauri polyfill layer (Phases 1-7 of Approach A3):\n\n**Polyfills:**\n- ProcessPolyfill: Node.js process object (argv, env, platform, versions, cwd, hrtime, cpuUsage, exit)\n- FileSystemPolyfill: fs module mapped to Mountain file:invoke commands\n- FileProtocolShim: vscode-file://, vscode-userdata://, vscode-resource://, vscode-remote:// protocol handlers\n- ChildProcessPolyfill: child_process spawn/exec/fork mapped to Mountain commands\n- IPCRendererShim: Electron ipcRenderer API with VS Code binary IPC protocol loopback\n- NativeModulePolyfill: require('electron') shim providing ipcRenderer, webFrame, app, screen, shell, dialog, clipboard, nativeTheme\n- SharedProcessProxy: Service proxies for extension host, search, debug, storage, update routing to Cocoon/Mountain\n\n**Services:**\n- DevLog: Tag-filtered development logging (vfs, ipc, config, etc.) with short/dedup modes\n- TauriMainProcessService: Drop-in replacement for ElectronIPCMainProcessService, routes getChannel().call() through Tauri invoke to Mountain\n- Trace: Zero-dependency browser tracing via performance.mark()\n\nThese polyfills enable VS Code to run in the Tauri browser environment without Electron.",
			"SHA": "0a0e5fda674c7d9c0b86bf6b59bc934c896fe793"
		},
